Remove the trailing vim.uv.run() from Server:start. Inside Neovim the server
handles already live on the editor's own event loop; the nested uv.run() never
returns (the listening socket keeps the loop active forever) and wedges the
main state machine -- keystrokes, RPC, autocmds, even SIGTERM stop being
processed while HTTP/websocket traffic is still served. Verified empirically
against the nixpkgs pin (0.9.6-unstable-2026-01-12); upstream main has since
removed exactly this call. Drop this patch when the nixpkgs pin moves past it.

--- a/lua/livepreview/server/init.lua
+++ b/lua/livepreview/server/init.lua
@@ -210,8 +210,6 @@
 		end)
 		table.insert(M.connecting_clients, client)
 	end)
-
-	uv.run()
 end
 
 --- Stop the server
